  "words": "public domain: anonymous, 18th century; printed 1894",
  "tune": "public domain: written about 1785 (Giuseppe Giordani died 1798, Tommaso Giordani 1806), as printed by Alessandro Parisotti in 1894 (Parisotti died 1924)",
  "arrangement": "original, written for Stackapella on the harmony of Parisotti's piano part (public domain: published 1894, Parisotti died 1924); the voice part is his, with breaths written in for beginners and the grace notes left out; Theodore Baker's English version (died 1934, also public domain) is not used: the song is sung in Italian only",
